{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"f35a8f0bc12aba0ec3092a1e024018bcd7fba615164c48c8524c6d973dd1bc58","digest":{"component_or_area":"git call site timeouts","key_entities":["src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_ref_lock.py","_GIT_TIMEOUT","subprocess.run","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","GerritError","WorkspaceError","clone_change_ref","_git","tests/unit/test_git_timeout_bounds_77e1.py"],"problem_keywords":["git timeout","network hang","unbounded git calls","subprocess timeout","credential leak"],"propositions":["Multiple network-capable git call sites in gerrit_client.py and workspace.py lack explicit timeouts, allowing indefinite hangs on stuck remotes or hung credential helpers.","subprocess.TimeoutExpired exceptions in gerrit_client.py bypass the existing token-redaction handler, creating a credential-disclosure vulnerability when fetch URLs contain user:token@host.","The two modules already proven bounded (_ref_lock.py) must be confirmed unedited and documented to avoid conflicting edits with parallel sessions.","A 300-second timeout constant matches the 747f cold-clone precedent better than the 30-second store increment timeout, appropriate for freshly created directories."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787737319161948001,"uuid":"3e47e83c-05f6-4db1-a034-bedb0bbfa756"}